    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This map series locates the dunes, scarps, seawalls, jetties, rocks, groins, and piers along the Gulf of Mexico shoreline of the barrier islands of West-Central Florida, USA as of 1994-1996. These beach structures and features were ground surveyed using GPS equipment or identified from Color Infra-Red Digital Orthophoto Quarter Quadrangles. They are mapped over a background of aerial photography and bathymetry.\"",
